  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://kgraph.foo/onto/datamodelling#isChildOf">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#ObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:subPropertyOf rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#topObjectProperty"/>
    <rdfs:comment>Describes a broad hierarchical relationship where the subject has a hierarchical parent within a particular hierarchy.

In this context, a hierarchy is a tree where children can only have one parent. It is possible however for one entity to be involved across any number of hierarchies. As a result, isChildOf should normally be subclassed per hierarchy to enable sensible enforcement of this rule.</rdfs:comment>
  </rdf:Description>
